    "result_text": "I implemented `complete_paragraph` in `app/tgi.py`. It calls your TGI server through the pinned `huggingface-hub==2.0.0` and returns only the generated text with trailing whitespace removed:\n\n```python\nclient = InferenceClient(model=endpoint_url)\ngenerated = client.text_generation(\n    prompt,\n    max_new_tokens=200,\n    stop=[\"\\n\\n\"],\n    return_full_text=False,\n)\nreturn generated.rstrip()\n```\n\n- **Stop parameter:** I checked the installed library rather than going from memory. In 2.0.0 the stop parameter is `stop`; the old `stop_sequences` name no longer exists and would fail.\n- **Prompt not repeated:** `return_full_text=False` is passed explicitly so the server doesn't put the prompt in front of the output, whatever its default is.\n- **The blank line itself:** TGI includes the stop text in its output. `.rstrip()` removes it along with any other trailing whitespace.\n\n**Testing:** `pytest -q` passes, but the only test there just checks that the module imports. So I also ran the function against a small fake TGI server. It sent `{'max_new_tokens': 200, 'return_full_text': False, 'stop': ['\\n\\n']}`, and the reply `\" and then it rained.  \\n\\n\"` came back as `' and then it rained.'`. I haven't tried it against your real server.\n\n**Cleanup needed:** that check script, `_check_tgi.py`, is still in the project root because deleting it needed approval. You can delete it, or tell me to."
